    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/5/75368.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 20,
    "turn_text": "So we we received an offer back from the governor with and there was a lot in it. And so we took that and we we've talked with our folks and our and our caucus and our comperese and to get a response where the house is. And so we're we're close to having something and then we have to go back with the Senate they've done the same and see if we can all come up with a response to send over to the governor hopefully here very soon to move this along. But I'll tell you it's it's a It's really a good budget that was passed by the Senate and passed by the house. The one passed by the house a little bit in the one Senate, but I think the combination as we make the sausage is going to be great because it doesn't make things speak. It's going to lower taxes. We've also put in their restrictions on a lot of these mandates and things the governor has sought to do. Put that in there. We've controlled spending, but at the same time, we've taken a lot of those funds that are coming in that we can use and putting in the things that are needed, like using one-time money for one-time spending things like fixing roads, bridges, infrastructure, broadband, et cetera. So really a lot of shared priorities, but the governor's got some entitlement programs he wants to talk about. He's not as keen on lowering taxes, and there's some different things he wants to spend money on. So we just got to work those things out. But I am optimistic that we will get to a budget because there's just too much This is a unique opportunity to do so many good things for the state and I think particularly if you contrast it with just the absolute goat rodeo of what's happening in Washington right now where you know these guys just can't seem to control their spending. They want to tax everybody, they want to punish folks and it's just absolutely ridiculous. So what I can tell folks is we're going to do a whole lot better job than the federal government, which I guess that's kind of set in the bar pretty low, but we're going to do a much better job than that. And I think folks will be very pleased with where we are and where we go with the funding. So but right now, the SAS and negotiations, you just having a lot of candid conversations to try to work through what can be some pretty sticky",
