    "turn_text": "yeah i i think if if i were the governor i would certainly be looking at it that way you know we passed The last full budget that we passed, we passed that over the objections of the governor. That lower taxes that spent money in the right areas, it did a lot of great things, produced regulations. We overrode the governor's veto. Then you look at the last session where we did not have the super majority to be able to overwrite his veto. Basically what we passed was a continuing resolution that essentially kept in place the Republican budget of the previous session during that second part during the, I guess the second half of his first term. So now we're in, he's in his, the first half of his second term now. And we would like to come up with something that he would sign that we can all agree on. But if not, we actually feel like we, I can tell you this in the house, we have the votes to override a veto if it happens. The Senate, I think, is a little closer call, but I think ultimately they do. So let's say that we did, let's say that the governor vetoed the budget We couldn't override. We ended up having to basically adopt another continuing resolution to take us into the next cycle. Well, the next budget cycle, just about anybody who follows politics with a degree, you're probably going to have just because of it being midterm elections, the party in power. And frankly, just how far to the left Joe Biden is going. It should be a strong election year for Republicans. And I firmly believe that you'll see super majorities of the House and the Senate. And so you could have yet another situation where Governor Cooper is confronted with the facts that he had when he first came to the Governor's match where he's dealing with a super majority Republican legislature that will be able to override his veto and thereby him having zero influence over eight years in the budget of the state. I don't think he wants that. I want to see us get something done and I think in the end that will be the key to seeing that we get a budget enacted.",
